WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.540
Surreal more than anything else.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.800
Feeling like I was in a dream I mean these

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.040
Movies are so big, the sets are so big

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.779
The costumes are incredible.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.040
Feels like you're inside a TV screen and then

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.260
There's the added part where you can't talk about it

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.220
So the end of your day, it's not
like you can call your mom and be like

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.180
"You'll never believe what I did
today."

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.560
So you just kind of delete it

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.060
So it feels like you're walking into a dream really.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.820
I guess pretty good.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.160
I just saw it the other day and
yeah, there's a lot of people going to dust

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.460
That's pretty sad.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.460
Because before you didn't have me.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.160
Yeah, you didn't.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.680
That's right so I guess it's pretty good.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.780
It's challenging because there are so
many characters but you know something

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.560
that we learned on Captain America: Civil
War, Joe and I

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.580
That movie was the first movie that we did

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:09.380
That had a really large number of characters in it

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.050
And what we realized as we were crafting
that movie was that it doesn't

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.749
Necessarily matter how much screen time that character has.

00:01:16.749 --> 00:01:18.100
It's just what you do with it.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.560
You know there's characters in
Civil War for instance

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:24.660
Like Spider-Man or Ant-Man, they didn't have a lot of screen time in that movie

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.240
But they were able to make a big impact and I think audiences were really able to

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.480
Enjoy and get a lot out of their time on
screen.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:35.400
So that's really how we try to balance and shape the movie

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.560
It's like we make sure that all the time that each character has

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.740
Is very meaningful, and
memorable, and exciting.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.420
I mean I... No.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.240
Because this is it, everything
we've got is in this.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:51.980
There will probably be

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:57.180
you know, a handful of deleted scenes on
the DVD but it's not many

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.760
I mean we really

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.640
We put everything, all the stories in there

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.320
We are done for now. We don't have any.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.140
I mean one of the creative upsides I think

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.640
In terms of how we approach this movie

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.980
Is we weren't thinking about the future.

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:17.740
There's no future for us right now in the MCU

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:21.900
And this story was since intended to be a conclusion

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.140
As opposed to a setup to something coming in the future

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.360
But we love Marvel

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.240
We love these stories

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:27.220
We love these characters

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.680
We've had the greatest run for the past seven years making these four movies

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:35.080
So with the right material, Joe and I
would certainly do another Marvel movie.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:41.220
I'm giving that one at 10.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:43.420
Have you worn that one?

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.700
I love that you got a nice little mini dress with a plunging neckline

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:50.400
And a belt

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.620
And a boot

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.940
Chic!

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.600
It's pretty awesome. That's my favourite one.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.580
10.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.160
So this is actually Hawkeye in the 1990s.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.380
Nice headpiece

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.980
I'm going to go with 8 for that one.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.000
Oh man I mean all... everytime you hang out with that guy

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.740
That guy... It's not even so much that I had like to sit down with him

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.260
But it's more every time I was just

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.720
thinking about him actually before you sat down

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.040
Said, "Wow I miss him."

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.880
And he's got such a

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.120
Like a cheeky smile on his face always

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.110
A very, very smart guy but he's got a

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:36.660
youthful spirit until his last moments
you know.

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:40.440
He's always... He has a fire in his heart, and he's a cowboy

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:43.840
It's in his body

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.040
This fortitude and strength.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.442
And he always had a smile on his face

00:03:47.442 --> 00:03:54.430
And his, you know, lightness to him that was infectious

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.820
That was every experience I've had with him

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:00.520
Always just such a wonderful, giving, thoughtful guy.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.760
I just had one experience but I'm so
grateful to have had that one.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.560
It's one of the many things that I think about

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.020
About this entrance into this Marvel Universe

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.920
That I had the opportunity to
have a cameo time with him

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.940
Yeah I mean, I just think it's with his
energy on set.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.200
When everyone would hear his voice

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.700
And it'll just like turn everyone
into kids again I think

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.140
You know there's a lot of movie stars that work on these movies but you know there was

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:34.700
More energy and excitement when Stan was on set than anybody.

00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:41.180
I remember our first cameo with Stan was on Winter Soldier

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.300
And I remember him coming to set that day

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.480
It was the first time we met him
and just the

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:50.920
Just having that first impression of him was so amazing.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.620
The way he came onto set

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.380
He just lit up the room

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:57.340
And the energy that he brought was amazing for his age.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.320
And I think I was so impressed with his level of enthusiasm

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.480
That he still was so

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:06.380
Passionate and excited to be telling these stories.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:11.200
That really struck me and stuck with me.

